      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name}: I think this still constitutes a bug, as avatars who's natural size is outside the scaling limits are stated to still be able to be their natural size\n\nThe current behaviour, introduced with avatar scaling, however, breaks pre-existing avatars who's natural size is < 0.1m (or > 100m)\n\nThis issue was fixed locally during the Avatar scaling beta, but failed to address the issue on the remote end. Giving that a fix was attempted in the past indicates that the current behaviour should be considered bugged",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
