  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-10-24T00:12:00.964Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "So I was testing avatar sizes with a friend of mine in VRChat and the normal limit for size is 0.2 meters when uploading avatars, Normally you cant go under this but we found avatars that were uploaded naturally smaler then 0.1, we found out that locally you yourself will be smaller then 0.1 but to others you will be set to 0.1 height. \n\nI understand the limiting of how big you get locally but I know alot of people and big communites who enjoy the Micro side of things and its very misleading when your small for yourself but not for others. \n\nThough the scaler system is now in VRChat, the community still made their own scalers that let you go smaller without assuminly editing the SDK to get it to work and this still happens.\n\nIm guessing this is a bug since no one really knows about it cause just a couple weeks ago people could see me really small below 0.1 height and head pat me correctly.\n\nAsking for this to get fixed for not only me but alot of my friends and community members to! World creators already have the power to limit the size you are in their own worlds so this shouldnt really be a thing im my opinon ^^\n\npls fix ;-; I need to be smol for comfort.",
